===== Reading of the result (by Claude; student must verify against the file) =====
Rule use-of-md5-digest-utils matches only the chained form DigestUtils.getMd5Digest().digest(...). Md5Crypt.java line 259 instead assigns the result: "final MessageDigest messageDigestMd5 = DigestUtils.getMd5Digest();" and calls update/digest on the variable later. The rule's shape does not match, so no finding.
Rule use-of-md5 matches MessageDigest.getInstance("MD5"), which does not appear in Md5Crypt.java.
Rule weak-random matches "new java.util.Random(...).method(...)" or Math.random(); Md5Crypt.java receives a Random as a parameter and never constructs one, so no match.
Rule md5-used-as-password matches MessageDigest.getInstance("MD5") followed by password use; not present.
Conclusion: Run A shows the rule and tool work (it hit the one expected line and skipped the two "ok" lines). Run B's zero is therefore a true zero for these patterns, not a non-functional tool, but it is a coverage gap for this file, because the file does use MD5 (lines 259, 275, 312).

